      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__uartns550_1ga6df754edf91aea638537a15536d4d34e" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>unsigned int</type>
        <definition>unsigned int XUartNs550_ReceiveBuffer</definition>
        <argsstring>(XUartNs550 *InstancePtr)</argsstring>
        <name>XUartNs550_ReceiveBuffer</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="struct_x_uart_ns550" kindref="compound">XUartNs550</ref> *</type>
          <declname>InstancePtr</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Receives a buffer previously specified by setting up the instance variables of the instance. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function is designed to be an internal function for the <ref refid="struct_x_uart_ns550" kindref="compound">XUartNs550</ref> component such that it may be called from a shell function that sets up the buffer or from an interrupt handler.</para><para>This function attempts to receive a specified number of bytes of data from the UART and store it into the specified buffer. It is designed for either polled or interrupt driven modes. It is non-blocking such that it returns if there is no data already received by the UART.</para><para>In a polled mode, this function only receives as much data as the UART can buffer, either in the receiver or in the FIFO if present and enabled. The application may need to call it repeatedly to receive a buffer. Polled mode is the default mode of operation for the driver.</para><para>In interrupt mode, this function starts receiving and then the interrupt handler of the driver continues until the buffer has been received. A callback function, as specified by the application, is called to indicate the completion of receiving the buffer or when any receive errors or timeouts occur. Interrupt mode must be enabled using the SetOptions function.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">InstancePtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the <ref refid="struct_x_uart_ns550" kindref="compound">XUartNs550</ref> instance.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The number of bytes received. </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
